      "source": [
        "## 5. Chi-square test\n",
        "H0: weather category and high hourly demand (>500) are independent. H1: they are associated.\n",
        "\n",
        "The lab teaches a goodness-of-fit statistic. For this question we use the same observed/expected formula and critical-value decision, with a 3×2 independence table. Expected counts = row total × column total / grand total; df = (3−1)(2−1). Weather: 1 clear/fair, 2 mist/cloudy, 3 adverse (original 3 and 4 combined)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 27,
      "id": "acad9f28",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "acad9f28",
        "outputId": "a5017663-d63e-42f1-dbdb-1019d4f84d20"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Observed frequencies:\n",
            " [[10408  1005]\n",
            " [ 4306   238]\n",
            " [ 1386    36]]\n",
            "Expected frequencies:\n",
            " [[10573.07   839.93]\n",
            " [ 4209.59   334.41]\n",
            " [ 1317.35   104.65]]\n",
            "Chi-square statistic: 113.63384265061639\n",
            "Degrees of freedom: 2\n",
            "Critical value: 5.991464547107979\n",
            "Reject H0: weather and high demand are associated.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Rows = weather groups; columns = demand <=500, >500\n",
        "observed = np.array([\n",
        "    [np.sum((data['weather'] == w) & (data['cnt'] <= 500)),\n",
        "     np.sum((data['weather'] == w) & (data['cnt'] > 500))]\n",
        "    for w in [1, 2, 3]\n",
        "])\n",
        "print('Observed frequencies:\\n', observed)\n",
        "row_total = np.sum(observed, axis=1)\n",
        "col_total = np.sum(observed, axis=0)\n",
        "total = np.sum(observed)\n",
        "expected = row_total[:, None] * col_total / total\n",
        "print('Expected frequencies:\\n', np.round(expected, 2))\n",
        "\n",
        "chi_square_stat = np.sum((observed - expected)**2 / expected)\n",
        "df = (3 - 1) * (2 - 1)\n",
        "critical_value = stats.chi2.ppf(1 - alpha, df)\n",
        "print('Chi-square statistic:', chi_square_stat)\n",
        "print('Degrees of freedom:', df)\n",
        "print('Critical value:', critical_value)\n",
        "if chi_square_stat > critical_value:\n",
        "    print('Reject H0: weather and high demand are associated.')\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('Fail to reject H0: insufficient evidence of association.')"
      ]
    },
