      "source": [
        "## Conclusion and limitations\n",
        "- The t-test checks mean daily demand; the chi-square test checks association, not causation. Both are classroom-level tests: consecutive days/hours can be correlated, and the pooled t-test assumes equal variances.\n",
        "- Monte Carlo estimates the chance of exceeding 500 and 800 rentals under the historical distribution. More trials reduce random sampling error, but do not remove dataset bias or predict changing future conditions.\n",
        "- The 2011–2012 data are historical, not current demand. Weather comparisons do not control for season or hour. No claim about shortages or station capacity is made.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    }
